e constants:\n  include/sodium/crypto_core_salsa20.h, crypto_core_salsa2012.h,\n  crypto_core_salsa208.h, crypto_core_hsalsa20.h, crypto_core_hchacha20.h\n\nEXACT list of exported symbols you must produce (verify with\n`nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -E 'salsa|chacha'`):\n\nsrc/crypto_core/salsa.rs (15):\n  crypto_core_salsa20 crypto_core_salsa20_constbytes crypto_core_salsa20_inputbytes\n  crypto_core_salsa20_keybytes crypto_core_salsa20_outputbytes\n  crypto_core_salsa2012 crypto_core_salsa2012_constbytes crypto_core_salsa2012_inputbytes\n  crypto_core_salsa2012_keybytes crypto_core_salsa2012_outputbytes\n  crypto_core_salsa208 crypto_core_salsa208_constbytes crypto_core_salsa208_inputbytes\n  crypto_core_salsa208_keybytes crypto_core_salsa208_outputbytes\n\nsrc/crypto_core/hsalsa20.rs (5):\n  crypto_core_hsalsa20 crypto_core_hsalsa20_constbytes crypto_core_hsalsa20_inputbytes\n  crypto_core_hsalsa20_keybytes crypto_core_hsalsa20_outputbytes\n\nsrc/crypto_core/hchacha20.rs (5):\n  crypto_core_hchacha20 crypto_core_hchacha20_constbytes crypto_core_hchacha20_inputbytes\n  crypto_core_hchacha20_keybytes crypto_core_hchacha20_outputbytes\n\nNOTE: core_salsa_ref.c uses a `crypto_core_salsa` macro/template expanded for\n20/12/8 rounds — read it carefully and reproduce all three variants exactly.\n\n`src/crypto_core/mod.rs` already contains `pub mod salsa; pub mod hsalsa20; pub mod hchacha20;`\n— do not change it.\n\nWhen done, report: the files you wrote, their line counts, and the output of\n`nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -cE 'crypto_core_(salsa|hsalsa|hchacha)'`.","agentId":"ab56613350f12f5a6","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All three files translated, compiling warning-free, and verified byte-identical against the compiled C reference.\n\n**Files written**\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-9qBOQP/translated_rust/src/crypto_core/salsa.rs` — 222 lines\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-9qBOQP/translated_rust/src/crypto_core/hsalsa20.rs` — 125 lines\n- `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-9qBOQP/translated_rust/src/crypto_core/hchacha20.rs` — 104 lines\n\n**Symbol count**\n```\nnm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -cE 'crypto_core_(salsa|hsalsa|hchacha)'\n25\n```\nAll 25 required symbols present (15 salsa + 5 hsalsa20 + 5 hchacha20), all `T` (global text). Note that identical bodies (e.g. the three `*_inputbytes`/`*_constbytes` returning 16) got folded to shared addresses by the linker, which is expected and harmless.\n\n**Implementation notes**\n- `core_salsa_ref.c`'s static `crypto_core_salsa(out, in, k, c, rounds)` is a private Rust `unsafe fn` taking `rounds: c_int`, called with 20/12/8 from the three public wrappers (the `#ifndef MINIMAL` block is unconditionally included since `SODIUM_LIBRARY_MINIMAL` is undefined).\n- The `j0 = x0 = ...` chained assignments are handled by computing the possibly-`c`-overridden constants first and then snapshotting into `j0/j5/j10/j15`; the `j`/`x` pairs are always assigned together in the C, so this is equivalent.\n- hsalsa20 keeps its C loop form (`for (i = ROUNDS; i > 0; i -= 2)`) and its distinct output layout (`x0, x5, x10, x15, x6..x9`, 32 bytes) versus salsa's 64-byte `x + j` output.\n- hchacha20's `QUARTERROUND` is a Rust `macro_rules!` mirroring the C macro exactly; all additions use `wrapping_add`, rotations use `crate::common::rotl32`.\n- `size_t` return values are `usize`; loads/stores go through the byte-wise `crate::common::{load32_le, store32_le}` (matching `NATIVE_LITTLE_ENDIAN` undefined).\n\n**Verification method** (worth noting for the caller): the crate's `target/release/libsodium.so` currently has unresolved symbols from other agents' in-progress files (`crypto_stream_chacha20`, `_crypto_stream_salsa20_pick_best_implementation`, etc.), so it cannot be `dlopen`ed yet. I instead compiled my three `.rs` file