es_block_decrypt _sodium_softaes_block_decryptlast\n  _sodium_softaes_block_encrypt _sodium_softaes_block_encryptlast\n  _sodium_softaes_expand_key128 _sodium_softaes_expand_key256\n  _sodium_softaes_inv_mix_columns _sodium_softaes_invert_key_schedule128\n  _sodium_softaes_invert_key_schedule256\n\nNote: softaes.c contains large lookup tables (SOFTAES_T0..T3 / Td tables etc.).\nTranscribe them EXACTLY — count the entries and double-check. Consider writing a\nsmall throwaway python script in $TMPDIR to convert the C array literals to Rust\narray literals rather than typing them by hand, then paste the result.\n\nIMPORTANT: some of these functions return a struct BY VALUE in C (e.g.\n`SoftAesBlock softaes_block_encrypt(SoftAesBlock block, SoftAesBlock rk)`).\nRust `extern \"C\"` with `#[repr(C)]` structs matches the C ABI, so declare them\nthe same way.\n\nWhen done report: the file written + line count + the output of\n`nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -E 'softaes' | sort`."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":457,"cache_read_input_tokens":216612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":457,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"548cc808-00d2-470c-b99f-a8d3e7e02fd0","uuid":"67a2799f-bbc6-4f8e-8d84-3ab8a648d0fc","timestamp":"2026-08-22T19:56:45.287Z"}
