no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_frombytes(h: *mut Fe25519, s: *const u8)\n    #[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_tobytes(s: *mut u8, h: *const Fe25519)\n    #[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\" fn _sodium_fe25519_invert(out: *mut Fe25519, z: *const Fe25519)\n\n(quirks.h maps `fe25519_frombytes` -> `_sodium_fe25519_frombytes`, etc. Those\nthree are the ONLY exported symbols from this file.)\nAlso provide safe wrappers `pub fn fe25519_frombytes(h: &mut Fe25519, s: &[u8])`,\n`pub fn fe25519_tobytes(s: &mut [u8], h: &Fe25519)`, `pub fn fe25519_invert(out: &mut Fe25519, z: &Fe25519)`\nso other Rust modules in this crate can call them ergonomically. Note the C code\nallows aliasing (e.g. `fe25519_mul(h, f, h)`), so your safe API should take\n`&mut` output plus `&` inputs by *value copies* where needed — the simplest\ncorrect approach is signatures like\n    pub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut Fe25519, f: &Fe25519, g: &Fe25519)\nand, at every call site inside this crate, callers may pass copies. To make\naliasing safe, take the inputs BY VALUE:\n    pub fn fe25519_mul(h: &mut Fe25519, f: Fe25519, g: Fe25519)\nUse BY-VALUE inputs (`Fe25519` is `Copy`, 40 bytes) for every fe25519 function\nthat has separate in/out parameters. Document this convention at the top of the\nfile. `fe25519_cmov(f: &mut Fe25519, g: Fe25519, b: u32)` and\n`fe25519_cswap(f: &mut Fe25519, g: &mut Fe25519, b: u32)` are the exceptions\n(cswap needs two &mut).\n\nCRITICAL CORRECTNESS REQUIREMENTS\n - Exactly reproduce every intermediate integer TYPE. The C code mixes\n   int32_t / int64_t / uint32_t / uint64_t deliberately (e.g.\n   `h0 -= carry0 * ((uint64_t) 1L << 26);` and `q = (19 * h9 + ((uint32_t) 1L << 24)) >> 25;`).\n   A wrong width or signedness silently changes results.\n   * `(int64_t) x * (int64_t) y` -> `(x as i64) * (y as i64)` (use wrapping_mul if\n     it could overflow in C's UB sense — it does not here, plain `*` is fine but\n     `wra