{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_mjbtvoufsyrrpmkk72xluzi6jbze4dldaigyoeo6b57xuq3pcnkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## What was written\n\n`/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-9qBOQP/translated_rust/src/crypto_core/softaes.rs` — **784 lines**, the only file touched.\n\nContains:\n- `#[repr(C)] pub struct SoftAesBlock { pub w0, w1, w2, w3: u32 }` (+ `Copy/Default`), plus the five `static inline` helpers from `private/softaes.h` as `pub` items: `softaes_block_load`, `softaes_block_load64x2`, `softaes_block_store`, `softaes_block_xor`, `softaes_block_and`.\n- Private items mirroring the C `static`s: `SBOX[256]`, `RCON[11]`, `INV_SBOX[256]`, `sub_word`, `rot_word`, `xtime`, `gf_mul_09/0b/0d/0e`, `inv_mix_column`, and the full SRM-1R set (`srm1r_dup16`, `srm1r_ror16`, `srm1r_ror32`, `srm1r_load_row_words`, `srm1r_store_column_word`, `srm1r_gather_row_bit`, `srm1r_pack_rows_bit`, `srm1r_spread_row_bits`, `srm1r_unpack_row_word`, `srm1r_pack_planes`, `srm1r_subbytes`, `srm1r_mix_columns`).\n- The 9 exported `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub unsafe extern \"C\"` entry points under their quirks.h linker names. Struct-by-value returns kept as-is (repr(C) matches the C ABI).\n- Convenience `pub fn softaes_block_{encrypt,decrypt,encryptlast,decryptlast}` Rust-callable wrappers so `crypto_ipcrypt` / `aegis128l` / `aegis256` can use them by path.\n\n## Key findings\n\n- **Which branch compiles:** with no `__wasm__` and no `FAVOR_PERFORMANCE`, softaes.c selects the `#else` branch — the SRM-1R bitsliced round. The 1024-entry `_aes_lut` table and the LUT-based `softaes_block_encrypt`/`encryptlast` are dead code in this configuration and are deliberately **not** transcribed. `HAVE_INLINE_ASM` is undefined, so the `__asm__ __volatile__` barriers in `softaes_block_encryptlast` are absent; `SOFTAES_STRIDE` stays 16, so the stride-scanned S-box copy (`t[4][16]`) is reproduced verbatim.\n- Wrap