/load_4)\n      crate::crypto_core::ed25519::ref10_tables::*  (FE25519_SQRTM1, ED25519_D,\n          ED25519_A_32, BASE, BASE2, ...)\n5. BYTE-IDENTICAL SEMANTICS: preserve evaluation order, the exact order of error\n   checks, integer wrap-around, truncating casts, signed/unsigned promotion, and\n   any BUG in the C. Never \"fix\" the C. Never add/remove a check.\n6. No new dependencies (offline).\n7. Only create/modify the files in YOUR ASSIGNMENT.\n8. Build check: `cargo build --release --offline 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error\" -A 12 | head -150`\n   Other agents write other files concurrently: IGNORE errors whose path is not\n   one of YOUR files.\n\n=========================  YOUR ASSIGNMENT  =========================\n\n  crypto_scalarmult/crypto_scalarmult.c                    -> src/crypto_scalarmult/mod.rs\n        (APPEND below the existing `pub mod curve25519; pub mod ed25519; pub mod ristretto255;` lines — KEEP THEM)\n  crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/scalarmult_curve25519.c     -> src/crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/mod.rs\n        (must start with `pub mod ref10;` then the translation)\n  crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/scalarmult_curve25519.h     (read: implementation struct)\n  crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/ref10/x25519_ref10.c        -> src/crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/ref10.rs\n  crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/ref10/x25519_ref10.h        (read)\n  crypto_scalarmult/ed25519/ref10/scalarmult_ed25519_ref10.c -> src/crypto_scalarmult/ed25519.rs\n  crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255/ref10/scalarmult_ristretto255_ref10.c -> src/crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255.rs\n\nHeaders to read: include/sodium/crypto_scalarmult.h,\ncrypto_scalarmult_curve25519.h, crypto_scalarmult_ed25519.h,\ncrypto_scalarmult_ristretto255.h, include/sodium/private/ed25519_ref10.h\n\ned25519 ref10 primitives (written by another agent, exported under these C\nnames — declare them yourself with `unsafe extern \"C\"`; ALWAYS check the real\nprototypes in include/sodium/private/ed25519_ref10.h):\n  _sodium_ge255