8_ciphertextbytes crypto_kem_mlkem768_dec\n  crypto_kem_mlkem768_enc crypto_kem_mlkem768_enc_deterministic\n  crypto_kem_mlkem768_keypair crypto_kem_mlkem768_publickeybytes\n  crypto_kem_mlkem768_secretkeybytes crypto_kem_mlkem768_seed_keypair\n  crypto_kem_mlkem768_seedbytes crypto_kem_mlkem768_sharedsecretbytes\n\nsrc/crypto_kem/mlkem768/ref.rs (5):\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_dec _sodium_mlkem768_ref_enc\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_enc_deterministic _sodium_mlkem768_ref_keypair\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_seed_keypair\n\nsrc/crypto_kem/xwing.rs (10):\n  crypto_kem_xwing_ciphertextbytes crypto_kem_xwing_dec crypto_kem_xwing_enc\n  crypto_kem_xwing_enc_deterministic crypto_kem_xwing_keypair\n  crypto_kem_xwing_publickeybytes crypto_kem_xwing_secretkeybytes\n  crypto_kem_xwing_seed_keypair crypto_kem_xwing_seedbytes\n  crypto_kem_xwing_sharedsecretbytes\n\nkem_mlkem768_ref.c is ~820 lines of ML-KEM (Kyber) reference code: NTT,\nMontgomery/Barrett reduction, polyvec compression, CBD sampling, rejection\nsampling from SHAKE128, indcpa keypair/enc/dec, and the FO transform. Translate\nit faithfully and carefully — every `int16_t`/`int32_t`/`uint16_t` cast matters.\n\nVERIFY: a reference build of the C library is at $TMPDIR/cbuild/libsodium.so.\nWrite a throwaway C harness in $TMPDIR that dlopen()s both that .so and\n<repo>/target/release/libsodium.so and compares, over many random seeds:\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_seed_keypair (deterministic from the seed) — compare the\n    full public and secret keys byte for byte,\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_enc_deterministic — compare ciphertext + shared secret,\n  _sodium_mlkem768_ref_dec — compare the recovered shared secret, including with\n    a tampered ciphertext (implicit rejection must match),\n  crypto_kem_mlkem768_* and crypto_kem_xwing_* seed_keypair /\n    enc_deterministic / dec, and crypto_kem_* front-end,\n  plus every *bytes() accessor.\nIf dlopen of the Rust .so fails with undefined symbols from other agents'\nunfinished files, build a tiny LD_PRELOAD stub .so defining them and preload it.\nReport the results, including the exact number of cases compared.\n\nReport: files + line counts + `nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -cE 'crypto_kem|mlkem768'`.","uuid":"5d50afe9-b891-4733-ba5b-e97067aee731","session_id":"548cc808-00d2-470c-b99f-a8d3e7e02fd0"}
