{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_zdewk6kxreykiuylbovt4epor73ugf5yvnyxpbwmeqze3qhn6fha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. All five files translated and verified against the reference C build.\n\n## Files written (absolute paths, line counts)\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-translate-9qBOQP/translated_rust/src/crypto_scalarmult/mod.rs` | 49 |\n| `.../src/crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/mod.rs` | 81 |\n| `.../src/crypto_scalarmult/curve25519/ref10.rs` | 236 |\n| `.../src/crypto_scalarmult/ed25519.rs` | 155 |\n| `.../src/crypto_scalarmult/ristretto255.rs` | 83 |\n| **total** | **604** |\n\n`nm -D --defined-only target/release/libsodium.so | grep -cE 'crypto_scalarmult'` → **21** (the assignment said \"17 total\", but the enumerated list itself sums to 21: 5+5+1+6+4; all 21 enumerated names are present, including the `D` data symbol `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_ref10_implementation`).\n\n## Translation notes\n- Took the `#else` branch of the `HAVE_TI_MODE` block: `fe25519_sub_lazy` == `fe25519_sub`. Took the non-`HAVE_AVX_ASM` path, so `_crypto_scalarmult_curve25519_pick_best_implementation` just re-assigns the ref10 pointer and returns 0.\n- `volatile unsigned char d` in `crypto_scalarmult_curve25519` reproduced with `ptr::read_volatile`/`write_volatile`; the return expression preserves the C integer promotion (`-(1 & ((d - 1) >> 8))` with arithmetic right shift on `c_int`).\n- `has_small_order`'s reuse of the loop variable `j` after the `j < 31` loop (i.e. `j == 31` for the masked top-byte comparison) is preserved verbatim, as is the `unsigned int k |= (c[i] - 1)` promotion/wrap (`(c[i] as c_int).wrapping_sub(1) as u32`).\n- `unsigned char *t = q` aliasing (curve25519 base, ed25519, ristretto255) is kept by writing through the raw `q` pointer rather than a local buffer.\n- `fe25519_*` aliased-argument calls (`fe25519_mul(da, da, a)` etc.) needed explicit `let x_v = x;` temporaries — Rust rejects `f(&mut x, x, y)` (E0503). `fe25519_invert(z, z)` uses the crate's `fe25519_invert_in_place`.\n- Error-check order in `_crypto_scalarmult_ed25519` (`is_canonical == 0 || frombytes != 0 || has_small_order != 0 || is_on_main_subgroup == 0`) kept with short-circuiting. Note the C also calls `ge25519_is_on_main_subgroup`, which was not in the primitive list I was given — I declared `_sodium_ge25519_is_on_main_subgroup` from `private/ed25519_ref10.h` + `quirks.h`.\n\n## Verification\n`src/crypto_core/ed25519/ref10.rs` is still a stub (owned by another agent), so the 9 `_sodium_ge25519_*` / `_sodium_ristretto255_*` primitives are undefined in the Rust `.so`. I built a `-rdynamic` C harness at `$TMPDIR/smh/harness.c` that defines forwarding stubs for every undefined `_sodium_*`/`_crypto_*_pick_best_*` symbol (dispatching via `dlsym` into the reference C lib, so the Rust wrappers run against the real ref10 primitives), then `dlopen`s `$TMPDIR/cbuild/libsodium.so` and the Rust `.so` and compares return codes, all 32 output bytes, and 32 guard bytes past the buffer.\n\nBecause the repo build is currently broken by other agents' in-progress files (`crypto_pwhash/argon2`, `crypto_kem/mlkem768`), I built from a byte-identical throwaway copy of `src/` at `$TMPDIR/smchk` (verified with `diff -r` that `src/crypto_scalarmult` matches the repo exactly).\n\nResult: **102,743 checks, 0 mismatches, 0 guard clobbers.** Coverage included constants/`primitive()`/`pick_best`, calling through the exported implementation struct's two function pointers, the all-zero public key, all 7 blocklist small-order points (plus high-bit-set variants), `p-1`/`p`/`p+1`/`p+2` non-canonical field encodings, the ed25519 order-1/2/4/8 torsion points, non-canonical scalars (`0`, `1`, `L`, `L-1`, all-`0xff`, `2^255-1`, high-bit-only), random garbage public keys, valid points generated via `*_base`, and single-bit-flipped valid points.\n\nHarness sensitivity was validated by injecting three deliberate bugs into the throwaway copy (`121666`→`121667` in the ladder; `t[31] &= 127`→`255` in ed25519; →`63` in ristretto255) — each produced mismatches, confirming the comparison is live for every backend.\n\n`cargo build --release --offline` reports **no errors or warnings** in any of my five files."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":105737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01CYCc4SXGc9AGQ43nZYyj8s","session_id":"548cc808-00d2-470c-b99f-a8d3e7e02fd0","uuid":"d5e5769c-3e46-4de4-a60f-2c884bc04d1a","timestamp":"2026-08-22T20:21:14.941Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Translate scalarmult modules"}
