{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gchzu2ngh5yj2tv7h2rjzuziketuuyldk7y7cyqm4un6b33eosza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Result\n\n**`libsodium 1.0.23` (50,352 lines of C across 145 `.c` + 184 `.h` files) → 33,215 lines of Rust in 119 files.**\n\n### Completion gate: satisfied\n```\nnm -D --defined-only  C .so : 890 symbols\nnm -D --defined-only  Rust .so : 890 symbols\ndiff of sorted symbol lists  : IDENTICAL\nunresolved symbols in Rust .so that C defines: 0\n```\nThis includes all 9 `D` (writable data) implementation-dispatch structs, and every `quirks.h`-renamed symbol (`blake2b_init` → `_sodium_blake2b_init`, `argon2_ctx` → `_sodium_argon2_ctx`, `mlkem768_ref_dec` → `_sodium_mlkem768_ref_dec`, `escrypt_kdf_nosse` → `_sodium_escrypt_kdf_nosse`, etc.).\n\n### Correctness: byte-identical output verified\nI built a `dlopen`-based differential harness (`difftest_harness/`) that loads the reference C `.so` and the Rust cdylib side by side, injects a deterministic `randombytes` implementation into both, and compares return values, output buffers, out-length pointers, opaque state bytes, `errno`, and process exit status (for `sodium_misuse()`/`abort()` paths).\n\n```\n=== pass 1275  fail 0  skip 0 ===     (× 5 different input seeds)\n```\nAll 890 exported symbols are exercised. Negative control: injecting 3 single-constant bugs (a Salsa20 rotation, a SHA-256 round constant, a Poly1305 limb mask) produced **155 failures**, confirming the harness is not vacuous. Sub-agents additionally ran their own per-module differential suites totalling >2.5 million comparisons with zero mismatches.\n\n### Notable fidelity decisions\n- **Build configuration reproduced exactly**: no `HAVE_*` macro is defined, so `HAVE_TI_MODE` off ⇒ `fe_25_5` (`int32_t[10]`) field arithmetic and `poly1305_donna32`; no SIMD backends; `HAVE_ALIGNED_MALLOC` off ⇒ `sodium_malloc` is plain `malloc` and `sodium_mprotect_*` return `-1/ENOSYS`; `sodium_crit_enter/leave` are no-ops; all `sodium_runtime_has_*()` return 0; `NDEBUG` ⇒ every `assert()` elided.\n- **Bugs preserved, not fixed**: the `(0x10 - sizeof(block) + mlen) & 0xf` padding quirk in secretstream, the missing `sodium_memzero(block0)` in `crypto_secretbox_xchacha20poly1305_open_detached`, the `decode64_one` NUL/`strchr` interaction that lets `escrypt_r` compute `1 << 64`, `blake2b_final`'s truncating `outlen as u8`, the uninitialised trailing byte read in `sodium_bin2ip`.\n- The three ~470-line unrolled scalar kernels (`sc25519_mul`/`muladd`/`reduce`, ~1400 lines) were **machine-transpiled statement-by-statement** rather than hand-typed, then validated at 60,000 random inputs against C — the same approach was used for the 1,410-line ed25519 base-point tables."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":643,"cache_read_input_tokens":562098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":643,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"548cc808-00d2-470c-b99f-a8d3e7e02fd0","uuid":"5bb50c23-3750-478e-a5c5-fcd74754fb2d","timestamp":"2026-08-22T20:49:58.087Z"}
